      "annotations": [
        "The agent presents a person token for this resource — the authorization endpoint requires one, in R3 exactly as in the base protocol (see Person Identity Access).",
        "It declares r3_operations: the vocabulary it is using (MCP) and the exact tool names it needs.",
        "The resource maps the requested tools to an R3 document and puts r3_uri and r3_s256 in the resource token. When it includes R3 information it MUST include both.",
        "r3_s256 is the SHA-256 of the exact bytes the resource serves at r3_uri, base64url without padding. There is no canonicalization step — verifiers hash the bytes off the wire.",
        "aud=AS URL means a four-party flow: the agent's PS federates with that AS.",
        "The agent receives a signed token but cannot fetch the R3 document — the resource serves it only to the AS or PS entitled to it. The agent carries the hash of a document it cannot read."
      ],
